eading\\\": \\\"Grounding Necessity Framework\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The grounding-necessity source supplies a conceptual contrast: a fact is fully grounded in a plurality only if the connecting question asking why the grounded fact obtains given those grounds lacks cognitive significance. It further links that lack of cognitive significance to Fine-style essential truths and uses the significance and essence principles to argue that full grounding metaphysically necessitates what is grounded.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Synthesis Boundary\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"This topic can compare empirical shifts in metaphysical commitments with a philosophical account of when explanatory dependence is objective and necessary. The support is cross-source but asymmetric: the psychedelic source gives evidence of belief change, while the grounding source supplies criteria for explanatory dependence rather than direct claims about psychedelic experience.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\\\",\n        \\\"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Metaphysical Belief Change and Grounding Necessity\\\",\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-metaphysical-belief-change-and-grounding-necessity\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-psychedelic-use-is-associated-with-significant-shifts-away-from-hard-physicalist--b7e61a4e9b3c\\\",\n        \\\"claim-greater-lifetime-psychedelic-use-correlates-with-stronger-baseline-panpsychist-b--a024d2968b54\\\",\n        \\\"claim-in-a-randomized-controlled-depression-trial-psilocybin-therapy-produced-shifts-a--7cfb0c0f75e7\\\",\n        \\\"claim-patients-who-clinically-responded-to-psilocybin-therapy-showed-greater-shifts-aw--b78b1f525f61\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-is-a-species-of-grounding-because-the-relation-between-a-truthmaker--4d84e79d3baf\\\",\n        \\\"claim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-a-species-of-grounding-in-which-a-truthmaker-grounds-t--9c9dc5afedc6\\\",\n        \\\"claim-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order-because-it-is-neither-transitive-irreflexive-nor--0dc6a102d51b\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-and-alethic-fact-grounding-are-non-asymmetric-because-distinct-propo--9d116dfbb4b5\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Non-Physicalist Commitments\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The psychedelic-belief source reports shifts away from hard materialism toward non-physicalist views and identifies baseline correlations between lifetime psychedelic use, stronger panpsychist beliefs, and weaker hard materialist beliefs. It also reports that psilocybin therapy, unlike escitalopram, produced shifts away from hard materialism in a controlled depression trial, with clinically responding psilocybin patients showing larger shifts than clinically responding escitalopram patients.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Truthmaking and Order Structure\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The truthmaking source treats truthmaking and alethic-fact grounding as species of grounding, then argues that grounding is not a strict order because it is not reliably transitive, irreflexive, or asymmetric. Its examples include mutual truthmaking or mutual alethic-fact grounding between distinct propositions or truth facts.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Synthesis Boundary\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"A synthesis-worthy page can examine how movement toward panpsychist, dualist, or other non-physicalist beliefs might interact with assumptions about what makes propositions true and how truth facts are grounded. The sources do not establish that psychedelic-associated belief change supports any truthmaking theory; they justify a conceptual comparison between altered metaphysical commitments and non-strict grounding structure.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\\\",\n        \\\"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Non-Physicalist Belief and Truthmaking Structure\\\",\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-nonphysicalist-belief-and-truthmaking-structure\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-shifts-away-from-hard-materialism-are-positively-associated-with-increases-in-ps--4bb5f88069f2\\\",\n        \\\"claim-perceived-emotional-synchrony-during-the-psychedelic-ceremony-mediates-later-cha--adcb9ca374b4\\\",\n        \\\"claim-ceremonial-psychedelic-use-increased-fatalistic-determinism-at-four-weeks-in-the--f71a027b70cc\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-combined-prospective-correlational-mechanistic-and-controlled-trial-evidence--bb114d52608c\\\",\n        \\\"claim-generalized-identity-is-a-non-factive-no-difference-operator-that-can-apply-to-f--7cb985988184\\\",\n        \\\"claim-grounding-and-essence-can-both-be-analyzed-in-terms-of-generalized-identity-yiel--e2abdab353f9\\\",\n        \\\"claim-necessary-entailment-or-equivalence-is-not-sufficient-for-essence-because-genera--162946956228\\\",\n        \\\"claim-full-generic-essence-is-captured-by-generalized-identity-being-f-is-what-it-is-t--96f5798ed301\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Experience and Well-Being\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The psychedelic-belief source links shifts away from hard materialism with increases in psychological well-being after ceremonies and reports that emotional synchrony during a ceremony mediates later changes in non-physicalist beliefs, with peer conformity moderating that pathway. It also reports a temporary overall increase in fatalistic determinism and notes that possible causal interpretation remains limited by sample selection and contextual confounds.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Generalized Identity Framework\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The generalized-identity source analyzes grounding and essence through a non-factive no-difference operator that can apply to factual and generic contents. On that account, full generic essence is captured by generalized identity, while necessary entailment or equivalence alone is not sufficient for essence because identity and grounding can distinguish essential structure from merely necessary coextension.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Synthesis Boundary\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"This topic can synthesize empirical change in metaphysical self-orientation with a philosophical framework for essence, identity, and grounding. The connection is conceptual rather than evidential: the psychedelic source does not use generalized identity, but its findings concern changed commitments about mind, matter, and reality that can be framed against a theory separating essential structure from mere modal equivalence.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\\\",\n        \\\"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Experience, Well-Being, and Generalized Identity\\\",\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-experience-wellbeing-and-generalized-identity\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p '/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/runs/run-20260426T152518Z--g2jrtnjpv1/semantic' && cat > '/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/runs/run-20260426T152518Z--g2jrtnjpv1/semantic/topic_generation.json' <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"topics\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-psychedelic-use-is-associated-with-significant-shifts-away-from-hard-physicalist--b7e61a4e9b3c\\\",\n        \\\"claim-most-psychedelic-associated-shifts-in-non-physicalist-metaphysical-beliefs-persi--9591d5bd7c0c\\\",\n        \\\"claim-participants-with-no-prior-psychedelic-experience-showed-larger-shifts-away-from--056a417d978d\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-combined-prospective-correlational-mechanistic-and-controlled-trial-evidence--bb114d52608c\\\",\n        \\\"claim-a-fact-p-is-fully-grounded-in-d-only-if-the-connecting-question-asking-why-p-obt--ea3a1a698124\\\",\n        \\\"claim-connecting-questions-lack-cognitive-significance-only-when-fine-style-essential--f96bc70d5d2d\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-conjunction-of-the-significance-principle-the-essence-principle-and-the-meta--4f212a9f1869\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-epistemic-constraint-on-grounding-does-not-undermine-grounding-objectivity-b--87922d9890f9\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Empirical Belief Movement\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"Psychedelic use is reported as associated with significant movement away from hard physicalist or materialist metaphysical beliefs and toward non-physicalist positions such as panpsychism, dualism, and non-naturalism. The same source reports that most of these non-physicalist belief shifts persisted for at least six months and that psychedelic-naive participants showed larger shifts than the full observational sample.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Grounding Necessity Framework\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The grounding-necessity source supplies a conceptual contrast: a fact is fully grounded in a plurality only if the connecting question asking why the grounded fact obtains given those grounds lacks cognitive significance. It further links that lack of cognitive significance to Fine-style essential truths and uses the significance and essence principles to argue that full grounding metaphysically necessitates what is grounded.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Synthesis Boundary\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"This topic can compare empirical shifts in metaphysical commitments with a philosophical account of when explanatory dependence is objective and necessary. The support is cross-source but asymmetric: the psychedelic source gives evidence of belief change, while the grounding source supplies criteria for explanatory dependence rather than direct claims about psychedelic experience.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-04-psychedelics-alter-metaphysical-beliefs--0d1ce18240f0\\\",\n        \\\"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Metaphysical Belief Change and Grounding Necessity\\\",\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-metaphysical-belief-change-and-grounding-necessity\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-psychedelic-use-is-associated-with-significant-shifts-away-from-hard-physicalist--b7e61a4e9b3c\\\",\n        \\\"claim-greater-lifetime-psychedelic-use-correlates-with-stronger-baseline-panpsychist-b--a024d2968b54\\\",\n        \\\"claim-in-a-randomized-controlled-depression-trial-psilocybin-therapy-produced-shifts-a--7cfb0c0f75e7\\\",\n        \\\"claim-patients-who-clinically-responded-to-psilocybin-therapy-showed-greater-shifts-aw--b78b1f525f61\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-is-a-species-of-grounding-because-the-relation-between-a-truthmaker--4d84e79d3baf\\\",\n        \\\"claim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-a-species-of-grounding-in-which-a-truthmaker-grounds-t--9c9dc5afedc6\\\",\n        \\\"claim-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order-because-it-is-neither-transitive-irreflexive-nor--0dc6a102d51b\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-and-alethic-fact-grounding-are-non-asymmetric-because-distinct-propo--9d116dfbb4b5\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Non-Physicalist Commitments\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The psychedelic-belief source reports shifts away from hard materialism toward non-physicalist views and identifies baseline correlations between lifetime psychedelic use, stronger panpsychist beliefs, and weaker hard materialist beliefs. It also reports that psilocybin therapy, unlike escitalopram, produced shifts away from hard materialism in a controlled depression trial, with clinically responding psilocybin patients showing larger shifts than clinically responding escitalopram patients.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Truthmaking and Order Structure\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"The truthmaking source treats truthmaking and alethic-fact grounding as species of grounding, then argues that grounding is not a strict order because it is not reliably transitive, irreflexive, or asymmetric. Its examples include mutual truthmaking or mutual alethic-fact grounding between distinct propositions or truth facts.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Synthesis Boundary\\\",\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"A synthesis-worthy page can examine how movement toward panpsychist, dualist, or other non-physicalist beliefs might interact with assumptions about what makes propositions true and how truth facts are grounded. The sources do not establish that psychedelic-associated belief change supports any truthmaking theory; they justify a conceptual comparison bet